{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And he blessed them.</b> The Sages have already said: 'Let not the blessing of an ordinary person be light in your eyes' (Megillah 15a). Yet Scripture recounts Laban's blessing of his daughters to teach that a father's blessing upon his children, given with all his soul, is undoubtedly more fit to take effect through the distinctive quality of the image of Elohim that blesses, as it says: כַּעֲבוּר תְּבָרֶכְךָ נַפְשִׁי (Genesis 27:4)."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {0 "The phrase הַמְבָרֵךְ is understood here as referring to the image of Elohim as the source that confers blessing; taken literally, 'that blesses.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:32:54.083484817Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}